ong.record-257bm-i-t7"],"evidence_ids":["mapping.long.record-257bm-i-t7"],"id":"long.record-257bm-i-t7","kind":"claim","label":"Long record Theorem 6.105 (Rationality through an integer recurrence)","locator":"Long record Theorem 6.105, p. 74, label record:257bm-i-t7","source_id":"paper.long.pdf","statement":"*Let $c:\\mathbb{N}\\to\\mathbb{N}$ satisfy $c(n)\\le n$ for every $n$. Then $\\sum_{n\\ge1}c(n)2^{-n}$ is rational if and only if there exist a positive integer $v$ and a sequence $u:\\mathbb{N}\\to\\mathbb{Z}$ such that\n$$\nu(N+1)=2u(N)-v c(N+1)\\quad(N\\ge0),\\qquad\n \\frac{u(N)}{2^N}\\longrightarrow0.\n$$\nThe limit condition is $u(N)=o(2^N)$; it does not assume that $u$ is bounded. No divisor-count hypothesis is imposed on $c$. Thus the ordinary statement also applies to $c=\\varphi$; the identification with the separate formal \\#249 development, including its indexing conventions, is not asserted here.*","status":"unverified"},"ref":"sha256:f31aeb6174afd909393ada9bc329cd29dc9b1b6a0de8f72a49f18ab372947af5/nodes/long.record-257bm-i-t7","relations":[{"derived":false,"family":"arguments","from":"sha256:f31aeb6174afd909393ada9bc329cd29dc9b1b6a0de8f72a49f18ab372947af5/nodes/long.record-257bm-i-t7","id":"sha256:f31aeb6174afd909393ada9bc329cd29dc9b1b6a0de8f72a49f18ab372947af5/edges/%5B%22long.record-257bm-i-t7%22%2C%22lean.Erdos249257.not_irrational_binaryCoeffSeries_iff_exists_temperedBinaryOrbit%22%2C%22formalizes%22%5D","kind":"formalizes","record_ref":"sha256:f31aeb6174afd909393ada9bc329cd29dc9b1b6a0de8f72a49f18ab372947af5/edges/%5B%22long.record-257bm-i-t7%22%2C%22lean.Erdos249257.not_irrational_binaryCoeffSeries_iff_exists_temperedBinaryOrbit%22%2C%22formalizes%22%5D","semantic_class":"formalization_correspondence","to":"sha256:f31aeb6174afd909393ada9bc329cd29dc9b1b6a0de8f72a49f18ab372947af5/nodes/lean.Erdos249257.not_irrational_binaryCoeffSeries_iff_exists_temperedBinaryOrbit"},{"derived":true,"family":"provenance","from":"sha256:f31aeb6174afd909393ada9